<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9128" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνοδος</span></b>  (B), ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>way up,</i> e.g. to the Acropolis
			at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.53
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἄ. οἰκοδομήσασα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>CIG</u>
					1948
				</span></i>
			 (incert. loc.): metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ εἰς τὸν νοητὸν τόπον τῆς ψυχῆς ἄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					517b
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>D.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>journey inland,</i> esp. into Central Asia, 
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάβασις, τριῶν μηνῶν
				ἄ.</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.50
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. παρὰ βασιλέα</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				51
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.1.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>rising,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ὑγροῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					355a6
				</span></i>
			; <i>rising</i> of a star, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηλυσίη τ᾽ ἄνοδός τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					536
				</span></i>
			; <i>slope of a hill,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				5.24.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> the first (or
			second) day of the Thesmophoria, <i><span class="en">
				Alciphr.
				3.39
			</span></i>, cf. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				86
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>ascent</i> of the soul to its original source, <i><span class="en">
				Hierocl.
				<u>in CA</u>
				24p.471M.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> Math., <i>increasing
				progression,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theol.Ar.
				58
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
